 "teaches": [
  "The whole step-explainer frame as a local component to copy: replace the titles, texts, shorts and the visual slot, and the buttons, dots and sizes keep working",
  "One tree for every shape: a visual box and a caption column in one box, with sizes and spacer lengths from windowWidth() and windowHeight(), so the drawing moves beside the caption when wide with no second copy",
  "Three captions per size: the full text, a short one, and only the step title at the smallest size, each an exact visibility on the step. Keep every string to its limit (params say which)",
  "A drawing with a regime for tiny sizes: below 70 dp the loop gives way to the current part's icon, which still reads",
  "Play without a clock listener: an eased value of a half-second tick drives repaints only while playing, and it is read in the dots' expression. Mono has no play button and no motion",
  "Publish the step from the component with {\"$name\"}: the local's own name is prefixed per call, so a slot could not read it otherwise"
 ],
