 "pitfalls": [
  "Walkthrough is the same frame without the adaptation: use it for a phone-size column, this for sizes under about 400 dp tall. Its buttons need more than 160 dp across and its caption and controls more than 160 dp down, and it has no place beside the drawing",
  "Do not name a variable step: it hides the step() function. Here it is stage",
  "A local of a component is prefixed per call and written in resources, where a slot's tree variable is not known yet: pass the eased step into a drawing through a canvas variable (g0 to g3 here) or a bound {\"$name\"} variable",
  "ifElse is (when false, when true, condition): ifElse(14, 15, step(@H, 300)) is 15 when tall",
  "IconButton filled with a runtime enabled keeps the onPrimary icon on its disabled face, which vanishes in mono: next is two buttons switched by visibility, filled and enabled, outlined and disabled",
  "Weights with no room left warn as zero size at 160 dp: the spacers between the buttons are exact widths, which may be 0",
  "A column with an exact height and a verticalWeight child took all the height there was in the C++ and TS players: size its children exactly"
 ],
